        {
          "question": "e-7651",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)^{3}-5 & >11 \\\\ 2(x-2)^{3} & >16 \\\\ (x-2)^{3} & >8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the cube root of both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{(x-2)^{3}} & >\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\ x-2 & >2 \\\\ x & >4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
